// =============================================================================
// 09: JAZZ JAM — SWING STANDARDS & BOSSA NOVA (Key of D / Bm — 112 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// Sophisticated, warm jazz backing track in the Key of D / Bm.
// Features authentic swing ride cymbals, walking upright bass, charleston
// piano comping, and full jazz improvisation roadmap.
//
// 🎸 HOW TO JAM OVER KEY OF D / Bm (ii - V - I - VI):
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// • The Harmonic Progression:
//    [Em7]   (ii)  -> E Dorian scale (E, F#, G, A, B, C#, D)
//    [A7]    (V)   -> A Mixolydian scale (A, B, C#, D, E, F#, G)
//    [Dmaj7] (I)   -> D Major / Ionian (D, E, F#, G, A, B, C#)
//    [B7]    (VI)  -> B Altered / B Phrygian Dominant (B, C, D#, E, F#, G, A)
//
// • 💡 THE GOLDEN JAZZ SECRET: "Target the 3rds on Beat 1!"
//    Chord tones sound 10x more melodic than running up and down scales:
//    - Over Em7   : Land on G  (3rd of Em)  -> Fret 8 on B string or fret 12 on G string
//    - Over A7    : Land on C# (3rd of A7)  -> Fret 9 on high E or fret 14 on B string
//    - Over Dmaj7 : Land on F# (3rd of Dmaj)-> Fret 11 on G string or fret 14 on E string
//    - Over B7    : Land on D# (3rd of B7)  -> Fret 8 on G string or fret 11 on high E string
//
// • B Minor Pentatonic (The "Cheat Code"):
//    Over all of this, B Minor Pentatonic (frets 7–10) sounds fantastic as it
//    outlines D Major Pentatonic (B, D, E, F#, A)!
//
// 🎛️ CONTROLS (<leader> = Space in Neovim):
//   <leader>ml : :StrudelLaunch (Connect to Strudel engine)
//   <leader>mp : :StrudelToggle (Play / Pause backing track)
//   <leader>mu : :StrudelUpdate (APPLY CHANGES LIVE — Press after uncommenting!)
//   gcc        : Toggle comment on a line (1 tap to introduce/mute a layer)
// =============================================================================


// =============================================================================
// 🎷 TRACK 1: "MANHATTAN MOONLIGHT" (Classic Swing ii - V - I - VI in D — 112 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// LIVE-BUILDING FLOW:
//   Starts with ONLY Layer 1 active (warm Rhodes 7th/9th jazz comping).
//   Play your melody, then introduce the jazz rhythm section layer-by-layer:
//   Line 53: Walking Bass | Line 56: Swing Ride | Line 59: Hi-Hat Foot | Line 62: Snare Ghost

stack(
  // [Step 1 - ACTIVE AT START] Warm Fender Rhodes Jazz Comping (Em9 -> A13 -> Dmaj9 -> B7b9)
  note("<[e3,g3,b3,d4] [a2,g3,cs4,fs4] [d3,fs3,a3,cs4] [b2,a3,ds4,g4]>")
    .s("triangle")
    .lpf(1100)
    .room(0.7)
    .decay(0.8)
    .gain(0.4),

  // [Step 2 - BASS] Authentic Walking Upright Bass with Chromatic Approaches (Press gcc here)
  // note("<[e2 g2 b2 d3] [a1 cs2 e2 g2] [d2 fs2 a2 ais2] [b1 ds2 fs2 a2]>").s("sine").lpf(360).gain(0.58),

  // [Step 3 - RIDE] Classic Swung Jazz Ride Cymbal (Press gcc here)
  // s("[ride ~ ride ride]").gain(0.35),

  // [Step 4 - HI-HAT FOOT] Acoustic hi-hat foot 'chick' on beats 2 & 4 (Press gcc here)
  // s("~ hh ~ hh").gain(0.3),

  // [Step 5 - BRUSHED SNARE] Soft brushed rimshot & snare ghost notes (Press gcc here)
  // s("~ rim ~ [~ rim]").room(0.5).gain(0.32),

  // [Step 6 - FEATHERED KICK] Subdued acoustic quarter-note jazz pulse (Press gcc here)
  // s("bd*4").lpf(180).gain(0.25),

  // [Step 7 - VIBES] Delicate vibraphone counter-melody (Press gcc here)
  // note("~ fs4 ~ a4 ~ cs5 ~").s("sine").room(0.6).delay(0.3).decay(0.4).gain(0.22),
).cpm(112)


